ent-WGMassTransceiver = mass transceiver
    .desc = A planetary uplink mast. Wolfgate's pull drags space-time around every world in the sector and scrambles ordinary radio below orbit, so this rig rides a world's signals on a mass-modulated carrier instead. With none running, nothing gets on or off the planet but handheld and crew radios.
ent-WGMassTransceiverBroken = wrecked mass transceiver
    .desc = { ent-WGMassTransceiver.desc } This one is torn open and dead. Five steel sheets, a screwdriver and a welder will get it back up.

wg-mass-transceiver-examine-up = [color=#3fe05a]It is transmitting.[/color] This world's comms are up.
wg-mass-transceiver-examine-down = [color=#ff3030]It is not transmitting.[/color] It has no power, so this world is cut off unless another transceiver is running.
wg-mass-transceiver-examine-broken = [color=#ff3030]It is wrecked and not transmitting.[/color] Patch it with five steel sheets, screw the panels shut, then weld the seams.
wg-mass-transceiver-examine-offworld = [color=#ffd23f]It is not on a planet[/color], so it has nothing to carry here.

wg-planet-comms-no-signal = No signal. This world's mass transceiver is down.
wg-planet-comms-no-uplink = No uplink. This world's mass transceiver is down, so a global announcement can't leave it.

guide-entry-wg-planet-comms = Planetary Comms

# The outpost every world has, where its mass transceiver stands.
